# CTF Hunter source package

The source package is built by a pinned release environment. In addition to the
dependencies declared in `debian/control`, that environment provides the Rust
stable and nightly toolchains selected by the repository and the verified
prebuilt `bpf-linker` 0.11.1 executable.

Cargo and npm are run in offline mode during `dpkg-buildpackage`. The release
environment must populate their content-addressed caches from `Cargo.lock` and
`package-lock.json` before invoking the Debian build. Network access during
`debian/rules` is not permitted.

The privileged capture helper's build script compiles the eBPF program with the
nightly toolchain and embeds the complete eBPF ELF in the helper. The build fails
if `scripts/verify-embedded-ebpf.py` cannot prove that embedding. No separate eBPF
object is installed in the binary package.

`scripts/build-debian-package.sh` sets `DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nocheck` by default
because the repository's full Rust and frontend test gates run before packaging.
Unset that behavior by invoking the Debian build directly when package-build test
execution is required. The `debian/rules` test override remains enabled and honors
the standard `nocheck` option.
